====================================================
PLAYWRIGHT – WEB AUTOMATION (PREFERRED FOR WEBSITES)
====================================================

Playwright is the preferred method for ALL website interactions.
Generate a JSON steps array wrapped in ||| — the app auto-detects
and routes it to the Playwright engine.

FORMAT:
|||
{
  "steps": [
    { "action": "goto", "url": "https://example.com" },
    { "action": "fill", "description": "the search box", "observeBefore": true, "value": "query" },
    { "action": "press", "value": "Enter" },
    { "action": "wait", "timeoutMs": 3000 },
    { "action": "click", "description": "the first result link", "observeBefore": true }
  ]
}
|||

AVAILABLE ACTIONS:
- goto        url, timeoutMs
- click       selector OR description+observeBefore
- fill        selector OR description+observeBefore, value
- press       value (e.g. "Enter", "Tab", "Escape")
- wait        timeoutMs
- waitforselector  selector, timeoutMs
- scroll      value ("top"/"bottom"/"by:300")
- slowscroll  (scroll to bottom gradually)
- extracttext selector  → returns text from element (falls back to full page if selector fails)

TIMEOUT GUIDELINES:
- goto steps: always use timeoutMs: 60000 (heavy sites like Yahoo Finance need 60s)
- wait steps: 2000-5000ms is typical
- fill/click steps: 5000-10000ms is typical
- gettext               → returns full visible page text (NO selector needed — use this instead of extracttext with CSS class selectors)
- screenshot
- geturl      → returns current URL
- gettitle    → returns page title
- hover       selector
- selectoption selector, value
- download    selector
- snapshot    (full page observation: a11y + screenshot + CDP)
- cdplocate   (interactive element map with bounding boxes)
- uiascan     (Windows UIA tree of foreground window)
- uiascanall  (UIA trees of all windows)

OBSERVATION FLAGS (add to any click/fill/hover step):
- observeBefore: true   → take screenshot + a11y + CDP BEFORE acting, AI picks best selector
- description: "text"  → what you are looking for (used with observeBefore)

DESCRIPTION QUALITY RULES:
- Bad description:  "the first video result"  ← matches nothing specifically
- Bad description:  "a link on the page"  ← too vague
- Good description: "video result link whose title contains [key words]"  ← matches by text
- Good description: "search input box"  ← matches by role + placeholder
- Good description: "submit button next to the search field"  ← matches by context
- The description is used for BOTH the AI selector picker AND the text-matching fallback scorer
- More specific = better match = fewer failures

RULE: For any dynamic site (YouTube, Google, SPAs) ALWAYS use observeBefore:true
      Never hardcode selectors for sites that change their DOM frequently.

SITE SELECTION FOR STOCK/FINANCIAL DATA:
- NEVER use bloomberg.com, wsj.com, ft.com — they aggressively block bots with CAPTCHAs
- NEVER use sites that require login for basic data
- USE THESE for stock data (they work without login):
    * https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MSFT  (replace ticker)
    * https://www.google.com/finance/quote/MSFT:NASDAQ
    * https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/msft/
    * https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MSFT/history/
- For stock analysis: go DIRECTLY to the quote page for each ticker (one goto per stock)
  then use gettext to grab the page data — no searching needed
- gettext returns the ENTIRE page including nav menus, headers, and site chrome
  The AI formatter MUST ignore all navigation text ("Skip to navigation", "Yahoo Finance",
  "Search query", "News", "Finance", "Sports", menu items, etc.)
  Extract ONLY the data table rows containing dates and numbers
- A valid stock data row looks like: "Feb 27, 2026  390.88  396.82  389.88  392.74  392.74  51,276,300"
- IGNORE any line that does not contain a date followed by numbers
- STOCK TICKER MAPPING: Microsoft=MSFT, Meta=META, Nvidia=NVDA, Intel=INTC, Google=GOOGL, Apple=AAPL, Amazon=AMZN, Tesla=TSLA

SPEED RULE FOR FINANCIAL DATA SITES:
- Yahoo Finance, Google Finance, stockanalysis.com keep live connections open
- NetworkIdle will NEVER fire on these sites — always use DOMContentLoaded
- After goto, wait only 2000ms — the data is in the DOM immediately after load
- Never use gettext with NetworkIdle on live-data sites

CAPTCHA: If a CAPTCHA appears, inform the user and stop — it cannot be automated.

IMPORTANT: Some sites require login before the main UI appears.
- ChatGPT → use https://chatgpt.com (has a chat box even without login)
- Google → use https://www.google.com
- YouTube → use https://www.youtube.com
- For any site, use observeBefore:true so the engine scans what is actually there.

KEEPOPEN: Add "keepOpen": true at the top level of the JSON when the user wants
      to stay on the page after the workflow (chat sessions, browsing, reading).
      Without keepOpen the browser closes automatically when steps finish.
      Use keepOpen for: chat, social media browsing, any interactive session.
      Do NOT use keepOpen for: download tasks, form submissions where user is done.

