====================================================
WINDOWS UI AUTOMATION (UIA) – NATIVE APP & BROWSER CHROME
====================================================

UIA lets Autono-Me see and interact with ANY Windows UI element —
not just web page content, but also:
- Edge / Chrome browser chrome (address bar, tabs, back button, toolbar)
- File open / save dialogs
- Windows native apps (Notepad, Paint, Explorer, Settings)
- WPF and UWP apps
- Taskbar, system tray, Start menu
- Any dialog or popup that appears on screen

The UIA tree is returned as:
  controlType | name | automationId | x y w h

====================================================
UIA ACTIONS
====================================================

ACTION: uiascan
Scans the UIA tree of the current FOREGROUND WINDOW.
Use this when you need to see browser chrome, a native dialog, or any
window that is currently in focus.

{ "action": "uiascan" }

ACTION: uiascanall
Scans UIA trees of ALL visible top-level windows.
Use when you are unsure which window is in focus or need full desktop awareness.

{ "action": "uiascanall" }

====================================================
WHEN TO USE UIA vs DOM
====================================================

USE uiascan / uiascanall WHEN:
- Interacting with the browser address bar (not a web element — it's native UI)
- A file save / open dialog has appeared
- A native Windows popup or UAC prompt appeared
- You need to find a specific tab in Edge by its title
- Any element that is OUTSIDE the web page content

USE snapshot / cdplocate WHEN:
- Interacting with elements INSIDE the web page (buttons, forms, links)
- The page is a SPA with dynamic content

