====================================================
WINDOWS SYSTEM TOOLS — ELEVATED DIALOG AUTOMATION
====================================================

When automating any Windows system tool launched with -Verb RunAs
(disk cleanup, disk management, chkdsk, defrag, etc.), follow this
generic pattern for navigating dialogs:

1. Launch elevated with Start-Process "toolname.exe" -Verb RunAs
2. Wait 5-7 seconds for UAC + tool to load (system tools are slow)
3. Use AppActivate by window TITLE (not process name) to focus each dialog
4. Use SendKeys {ENTER} to accept default/OK buttons
5. Use {TAB}{ENTER} to reach non-default buttons (e.g. "Delete Files")
6. Between dialogs, always add Start-Sleep -Seconds 2 minimum
7. After the final action, wait long enough for the tool to finish
   (disk scans can take 10-30 seconds — use Start-Sleep -Seconds 15)

WINDOW TITLE DETECTION:
- Use AppActivate with the exact window title as it appears on screen
- If unsure of title, use a partial match: try { AppActivate("Disk") } catch {}
- Always wrap AppActivate in try/catch — the window may not be ready yet

EXAMPLE PATTERN (any elevated system tool with OK dialogs):
Start-Process "toolname.exe" -Verb RunAs
Start-Sleep -Seconds 6
Add-Type -AssemblyName Microsoft.VisualBasic
Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms
try { [Microsoft.VisualBasic.Interaction]::AppActivate("Dialog Title") } catch {}
Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 500
[System.Windows.Forms.SendKeys]::SendWait("{ENTER}")
Start-Sleep -Seconds 12
try { [Microsoft.VisualBasic.Interaction]::AppActivate("Main Window Title") } catch {}
Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 500
[System.Windows.Forms.SendKeys]::SendWait("{ENTER}")
Start-Sleep -Seconds 2
try { [Microsoft.VisualBasic.Interaction]::AppActivate("Confirmation Title") } catch {}
Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 500
[System.Windows.Forms.SendKeys]::SendWait("{TAB}{ENTER}")
Start-Sleep -Seconds 15
Write-Output "Tool completed successfully"

NEVER leave a window in its default size. ALWAYS maximize.